From 4d57f296df8e5ef853e660b467f866985d795c92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: add Maxim MAX77705 USB Type-C/PD and MUIC driver

Driver for the firmware-driven USB Type-C / Power Delivery controller
and D+/D- switch of the MAX77705 PMIC (Galaxy S10 family), talking to
its firmware through the opcode interface, with its binding.

 - Type-C port with orientation, data and power role reporting, role
   switch and VBUS (OTG) control through the charger's OTG regulator;
   the CC role bits follow the port type.
 - PD: role swaps, optional DR_Swap to host as a sink (prefer_host),
   input current limit from the PD contract (chg_icl, chg_icl_max_ma),
   OTG current limit (otg_ma).
 - DisplayPort alternate mode (altmode): lanes and HPD are routed
   after the Configure ACK and every DP status update is passed to the
   muxes.
 - The init sequence sends the opcodes the vendor driver sends at
   probe (CC/SBU short detection, AUTOIBUS, CCCTRL1 with the debug and
   audio accessory bits, CC lock-error clear, alternate mode); the
   alternate mode opcode is what makes the firmware attach OTG
   adapters.
 - The interrupt registers are also polled once a second, and the host
   role is re-asserted after a DWC3 rebind. Firmware restarts are
   handled; the work runs on a freezable workqueue.
 - debugfs: a state file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
